WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.210
- And what was happening in
that scene? Was that a sinkhole?

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:03.323
- That was.

00:00:03.323 --> 00:00:05.120
- That's my worst--not my worst nightmare.

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.260
It's definitely in the top three.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:08.370
- Yeah, no. I didn't have that
fear until I did the show.

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:09.630
And then I was like, "Oh."

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:11.210
Don't do research into
it. Do not do research.

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.800
- I have. I have Googled
the hell out of it

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.640
'cause it happened in Florida
and I was like, "Wait, what?"

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:16.870
I was like--no, it
happens. It just happens.

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:17.703
- [Zyra] Yeah, I don't like that.

00:00:17.703 --> 00:00:19.810
- Yeah. And you just don't know.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:22.420
Yeah. Anyway, it terrifies me.

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:25.100
That will give me nightmares
for at least week.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.230
Yeah, for at least a week.

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:27.580
Okay. Well, there's other
things that will happen

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:28.480
that will probably give me nightmares.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:29.707
- Probably.

00:00:29.707 --> 00:00:30.620
- But you're the first amputee to star

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:32.879
in a primetime network
show, so that's pretty cool.

00:00:32.879 --> 00:00:33.933
It's amazing.

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:37.158
(audience cheers) Yeah. For
a lot of people who think,

00:00:37.158 --> 00:00:38.950
"Oh, I can't do that" or it's
not the norm, or whatever.

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:41.430
That's amazing, that you get
to be the pioneer of that.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:42.510
- See, I've never felt like that.

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:44.890
None of my family is like that.

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:48.380
Their like, "You're fine.
Come with the rest of us.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:50.100
You still have to carry things."

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.697
Like my mother, growing up, she was like,

00:00:51.697 --> 00:00:53.320
"Alright, I'm gonna give you muscles."

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:56.070
And so I would be the one to
carry all the grocery bags in.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:56.903
- [Kelly] Amen.

00:00:56.903 --> 00:00:57.736
- Even after I had my leg cut off,

00:00:57.736 --> 00:00:59.430
she was like, "Alright,
grocery bags, let's do it."

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:01.540
- Oh my God, I love that
though. It pushes you.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:02.686
- [Zyra] Oh yeah.

00:01:02.686 --> 00:01:04.410
- Yeah. Oh, and I make my
kids do that stuff, too.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:07.542
I'm like, "You don't even
pay rent, so grab something."

00:01:07.542 --> 00:01:08.750
(audience laughs)

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:12.370
- If you don't pay rent, you
have to carry grocery bags.

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:13.203
- Well, you have some special guests

00:01:13.203 --> 00:01:14.420
who came to support you, right?

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:15.253
- I do.

00:01:15.253 --> 00:01:16.510
- Can you point 'em out for us?

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:17.343
- Right there.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:18.858
- Right here? Yes!

00:01:18.858 --> 00:01:19.900
(audience cheers)

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:22.750
I love that. So wait, you got into acting

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:24.590
because of your limb difference. Right?

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:25.423
- Yeah.

00:01:25.423 --> 00:01:26.322
- So how? Like why?

00:01:26.322 --> 00:01:28.893
- So before that, I
wanted to be a mortician.

00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:31.203
- Is that real?

00:01:31.203 --> 00:01:32.036
- Yeah, that's real.

00:01:32.036 --> 00:01:33.150
- I love that.

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:34.270
- I'm not kidding you. I
wanted to be a mortician.

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:36.195
- You could still play a mortician.

00:01:36.195 --> 00:01:37.142
- I could.

00:01:37.142 --> 00:01:38.129
- Absolutely.

00:01:38.129 --> 00:01:40.848
- [Logan] If you can be on this show,

00:01:40.848 --> 00:01:42.020
you can be whatever you want.

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:44.783
- I feel you like, you
gotta do research into that.

00:01:44.783 --> 00:01:46.063
Then it's basically, like,
getting your degree. Right?

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.130
- [Cynthia] You can do it.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:51.360
- I had my leg cut off, right?

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.550
And I was like, "I wanna inspire people."

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:56.830
Which now makes me, like,
inspire grosses me out now.

00:01:56.830 --> 00:01:58.330
The word 'cause everybody
uses it for like,

00:01:58.330 --> 00:01:59.620
the littlest things or like...

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:01.500
- Oh, I love the word inspire.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:03.770
- Okay, but use it in a different way.

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:05.237
People use it on amputees and their like,

00:02:05.237 --> 00:02:07.890
"You picked a flower.
You're so inspirational."

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:10.867
- Oh, well okay. I gotcha. I got you.

00:02:10.867 --> 00:02:12.769
- [Zyra] Nothing inspirational,
just living life.

00:02:12.769 --> 00:02:13.602
- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:13.602 --> 00:02:15.780
- So I was like, I wanna inspire
people. I wanna be a model.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:18.080
I'm gonna show people you
can do whatever you want.

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:20.080
And then I went out, I got an agent.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:21.027
And she was like,

00:02:21.027 --> 00:02:22.930
"Alright, we're gonna
send you on acting things

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:24.712
'cause you gotta big personality."

00:02:24.712 --> 00:02:27.870
And then I just kept
doing them and doing them

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:28.990
and I was absolutely terrified.

00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:31.760
Like I would get violently
ill before every audition.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:33.560
- Did you ever turn
around and wear a hoodie

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:34.853
and like, hide yourself.

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:38.738
- There's no shame here. No shame.

00:02:38.738 --> 00:02:40.120
- [Zyra] I respect that. I respect that.

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:42.198
- But those moments mold
us. They build character.

00:02:42.198 --> 00:02:44.140
That's what I've been
told by my therapist.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:47.568
- Yeah, for sure. It's the
trauma, it makes you funny.

00:02:47.568 --> 00:02:49.020
- Yes, it makes the humor.
You gotta find humor.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:51.010
So I heard you have a
certain tattoo. What is it?

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:52.770
- I do. It's on my foot.
I would show you, but--

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:54.532
- Then you have to take it all off.

00:02:54.532 --> 00:02:55.730
- Yeah, it'd be a whole thing.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:57.523
So, when I was in the
hospital, right, 13 years old.

00:02:57.523 --> 00:03:00.070
We have a really sick sense of humor.

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:01.980
And so I have one foot in the grave

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:05.270
written on my leg in
permanent marker by my aunt.

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:06.818
And so I was in Australia, right,

00:03:06.818 --> 00:03:07.660
and I was like, "I wanna get a tattoo."

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:09.890
'Cause it's Australia,
I wanna do fun things.

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:12.840
And so I had her send me her writing.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:14.930
One foot in the grave and I
got it tattooed on my foot.

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:16.948
- That's actually very sweet.

00:03:16.948 --> 00:03:19.392
And inspirational.

00:03:19.392 --> 00:03:20.447
- [Zyra] Inspirational.

00:03:20.447 --> 00:03:21.534
- Inspirational.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.037
- I was goin' for sick humor,
but okay. That works too.

00:03:23.037 --> 00:03:24.380
- But that's inspirational.

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:25.970
It's like finding the humor in that.

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:27.575
I love your family.
Your family is awesome.

00:03:27.575 --> 00:03:28.797
- [Zyra] My family is great.

00:03:28.797 --> 00:03:31.520
- Do y'all have any tattoos
that mean something?

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:32.520
- Oh, no, no, no.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.850
Lynda Browning would not
let me get any tattoos

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:36.280
and I still am afraid of my mother.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:37.547
- Do you have any?

00:03:37.547 --> 00:03:38.611
- [Marque] I got two.

00:03:38.611 --> 00:03:40.412
- You've got two?
- Can't show you all of 'em.

00:03:40.412 --> 00:03:41.245
I'm just kidding.

00:03:41.245 --> 00:03:43.970
One here on my arm,

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:48.563
was actually done my friend
who just passed from COVID.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:50.700
- [Kelly] I'm so sorry, but man,

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:51.920
what a beautiful thing to have.

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:53.620
That legacy on your arm from, yeah.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:56.568
- Yeah, it says, "Breathe.
This too shall pass."

00:03:56.568 --> 00:03:57.918
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:03:57.918 --> 00:04:00.620
- And then another one that's
over here. It doesn't matter.

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:03.193
It's like sun rays and space and whatever.

00:04:04.171 --> 00:04:07.004
(audience cheers)

00:04:10.442 --> 00:04:11.942
- Oh, that's cool.

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:15.543
- Inspiration, all the things.

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:19.193
- I love that.

